in @glass

# Property: substrate source lives in `shards/`, not `boot/std/`, not
# `glass/`. This property names the rule that drives the
# `boot/std/*` → `shards/*` migration via the kintsugi loop.
#
# Per Alex's 2026-06-17 question — "How can we use kintsugi to migrate
# the old bootstrap into the new shape?" — the answer is mechanical:
# declare the rule here; every kintsugi pulse on the corpus reads
# this property and surfaces each offending `boot/std/*.mirror` file
# as a dark region; the fracture body (forward-promised at
# `@kintsugi/fracture/substrate_source_in_shards`) carries the
# opacity_map into migration morphisms (mv + keyword rewrite +
# namespace rewrite).
#
# === Recognition shape ===
#
# Per [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]: "Mirror source
# lives in shards/ (not boot/, not glass/). Substrate source IS
# substrate data; the recursive proof is literal. Use existing
# substrate vocabulary; 'glass' was an external metaphor superseded
# immediately."
#
# Mara's `keyword_matches_path_root` rename closure (mirror commit
# `d498fc0`, 2026-06-16) proved the kintsugi-driven migration pattern
# for 7 shards under `shards/epistemologic/property/` →
# `shards/epistemologic/pact/`. This property generalizes the pattern
# to ALL `boot/std/*` shards: the same kintsugi loop, the same
# opacity-map carrier, the same `splinter(ast)` morphism discharge.
# Different scope; same shape.
#
# === Self-witnessing ===
#
# This shard MUST live at
# `shards/epistemologic/pact/substrate_source_in_shards.mirror` and
# declare with `pact`. It satisfies its own rule on the first frame.
# Landing it under `boot/std/` would violate the rule it declares —
# the test `does_NOT_live_under_boot_std` in
# `bootstrap/tests/substrate_source_in_shards_substrate.rs` enforces
# this.
#
# === Operational discharge ===
#
# Mara's cross-shard resolver (mirror commit `128e0d2`, the @io
# floor that walks `shards/` + `boot/std/` and builds the
# declared-namespace index) is the natural discharge surface. The
# sibling-tick extension: count each declaration whose source file
# lives under `boot/std/` as an additional dark axis. The dark count
# grows; the corpus verdict downgrades from `success` to
# `failure(opacity_map)`. Each opacity names one offending file
# plus the migration morphism the fracture body should apply.
#
# Auto-apply has two paths:
#
#   (a) Substrate-clean: blocked on `@mirror/fracture/predicate`
#       (task #272, liquid-type predicates inferred via sheaf-
#       diffusion Houdini fixpoint). When that lands, fracture
#       bodies discharge declaratively via `splinter(ast)`; the
#       kintsugi loop reads the opacity_map and runs them.
#
#   (b) Practical: a Rust @io fracture body, parallel to how
#       `collect_declared_namespaces` was the @io floor for
#       `composition_closed`. Reed designs `mirror kintsugi --apply`
#       — reads opacity_map, looks up the fracture body, runs the
#       morphism, commits the migration.
#
# Per [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]: declarative
# property half lands here; operational discharge half is the
# resolver extension + the eventual fracture body.
#
# === Migration inventory (per Taut 2026-06-17) ===
#
# Stuck under `boot/std/`:
#
#   - 17 shards in `boot/std/epistemologic/property/*` using the
#     retired `grammar` keyword and the old `property` path segment
#     (autopoietic, content_addressed, frame_relativity, glass_wall,
#     halts, io_safety, is_prism_record, total_classification,
#     coincidence_matches, duplicate_variant, filename_matches_glass,
#     plus laws/{causality, duration_algebra, functor, monad,
#     monoidal, monotonicity}).
#
#   - ~22 active importers in `boot/std/` + `shards/` that reference
#     these old paths via `in @epistemologic/property/<X>`.
#
#   - 5 Rust string constants in
#     `bootstrap/src/{property,score,kintsugi,tensor,oscillate}.rs`
#     hardcoding `@epistemologic/property/total_classification` and
#     similar.
#
#   - The 12 shards under `shards/epistemologic/pact/` were already
#     migrated by Mara's `d498fc0` closure + Taut's `ac34e55`
#     (benchmark.mirror lift). They satisfy this property today.
#
# === Form-side discipline ===
#
# This property sits at the form-side of the form/process partition
# ([[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]; the
# @mirror = form, @kintsugi = process partition). The rule names
# WHAT must hold across the source-location axis; the realisation
# lives at `@kintsugi/fracture/substrate_source_in_shards`
# (forward-promised); the operator of the bridge is the kintsugi
# loop (substrate-pull).
#
# === Verdict surface ===
#
# Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
#   success              -- every declaration in the corpus is
#                          sourced from `shards/`. No boot/std
#                          declarations remain.
#   failure(opacity_map) -- one or more declarations live under
#                          `boot/std/`; each opacity names ONE
#                          offending file path plus the suggested
#                          target path under `shards/`.
#   partial(opacity_map) -- mixed corpus state — some files
#                          migrated, some still pending. Typically
#                          mid-cascade.
#
# Located transparency (not @glass.verdict): the kintsugi loop
# consumes the opacity_map to direct migration. The fracture body
# (forward-promised) emits the morphism that proposes
# `git mv boot/std/<X>.mirror shards/<X>.mirror` plus the in-file
# keyword + namespace rewrite, plus the import sweep across
# consumers. The property names the rule; the fracture realises it;
# the kintsugi loop is the bridge.

pact @epistemologic/pact/substrate_source_in_shards {
  # The set of declared namespaces whose source file lives under
  # `boot/std/`. Parallel to `collect_declared_namespaces` but
  # filtered on the source-path axis: for each concrete top-level
  # `glass | prism | pact @<X>` declaration in the corpus, include
  # `@<X>` iff its containing file's path is rooted at `boot/std/`.
  #
  # Multiplicity: one entry per declaration. Two declarations of
  # `@<X>` (one in shards/, one in boot/std/) yield exactly one
  # entry — the boot/std/ one — since that's the offender.
  #
  # This is the OFFENDER set. `substrate_source_in_shards(corpus)`
  # succeeds iff this set is empty.
  boot_std_declarations(corpus: ref) -> [ref] { \ }

  # The combined property: `substrate_source_in_shards(corpus)` is
  # success iff `boot_std_declarations(corpus)` is empty.
  #
  # Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
  #   success              -- every declaration sourced from shards/.
  #   failure(opacity_map) -- some declarations live under boot/std/;
  #                          each opacity names ONE offending file +
  #                          the suggested shards/ target path.
  #   partial(opacity_map) -- mid-cascade mixed state.
  substrate_source_in_shards(corpus: ref) -> transparency { \ }
}

out boot_std_declarations
out substrate_source_in_shards
out @epistemologic/pact/substrate_source_in_shards
